---
// firma2-record-bar — the record's OWN bar, under the app's top bar: the row
// Linear puts under its breadcrumbs, with the record's views on the left
// (Overview · Activity · Issues there) and the sidebar's icons on the right
// (user, 2026-10-22: "the project detail page within has a top bar, and some
// icons on this top bar control the right side rail").
//
// NOT THE APP'S TOP BAR. firma2-top-bar is the app's chrome — the way out and
// the things you do with the page — and stays exactly as it was. This row
// belongs to the record, spans the main column and the rail, and pins under
// that bar so it never scrolls away: a closed rail leaves nothing behind
// (firma2-rail `external`), so the way back has to be somewhere that is always
// on screen.
//
// NO SEAM. Same surface as the page, no hairline: it reads as the top of the
// record, not as a second band of chrome. It does carry the page's background,
// because content scrolls under it.
//
// THE RAIL STARTS UNDER IT. Present, it publishes --firma2-record-bar-height
// on the scrolling pane, which every pinned rail (firma2-rail) and docked
// sheet (bcn-side-sheet) adds to the app bar's height, and --firma2-rail-lift:
// 0, because the rail no longer reaches up through the pane's padding to meet
// the app bar — this row is what it meets.
//
// SLOTS: default (start — the record's views, none yet), "end" (the rail's
// icons, firma2-rail-modes). With nothing to show — no views, and the rail
// unpinned under the content on a tablet or phone — the row steps out.
//
// bcn-lego-checked: no esa- lego is a sticky in-page row (esa-app-bar is the
// app's band, and the app already has one — firma2-top-bar; esa-tab-layout is
// a tab strip with panels, and this row has no tabs yet). Layout is `.repel`;
// the controls in it are esa-buttons. Beacon is not cloned on this machine.
---
<div class="firma2-record-bar repel" data-record-bar>
  <div class="firma2-record-bar__start cluster" data-gap="xs"><slot /></div>
  <div class="firma2-record-bar__end cluster" data-gap="xs"><slot name="end" /></div>
</div>

<style>
  .firma2-record-bar {
    --_pad: var(--firma2-pane-padding, var(--spacing-500, 1.5rem));
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--firma2-sticky-origin, 0px) + var(--firma2-band-height, 48px));
    z-index: var(--z-header, 200);
    flex-wrap: nowrap;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    block-size: 2.5rem;
    /* Up through the pane's top padding to meet the app bar, and out through
       its side padding so the row spans the pane, rail included. */
    margin-block-start: calc(var(--_pad) * -1);
    margin-inline: calc(var(--_pad) * -1);
    padding-inline: var(--_pad);
    background: var(--firma2-sheet-background, var(--color-background-default, #fcfcfc));
  }
  .firma2-record-bar__end {
    flex-wrap: nowrap;
  }

  /* Nothing to show: no views on the left, and the rail's icons have stepped
     out because the rail is under the content (firma2-rail-modes sets
     data-idle). An attribute, not a nested :has() — CSS refuses :has() inside
     :has(), and drops the whole rule. */
  .firma2-record-bar[data-idle]:not(:has(.firma2-record-bar__start > *)) {
    display: none;
  }

  /* What the pinned rails and docked sheets read (see the header). */
  :global(.esa-app-shell__content:has(> .firma2-record-bar:not([data-idle]))) {
    --firma2-record-bar-height: 2.5rem;
    --firma2-rail-lift: 0px;
    /* The rail reaches up behind this row (firma2-rail's head), so its icons
       sit on the rail's surface; its content starts a short step below them. */
    --firma2-rail-head: 2.5rem;
    --firma2-rail-head-gap: var(--spacing-300, 0.75rem);
  }

  /* With the rail behind it, the row is transparent and above the rail, so
     the icons paint on the rail's surface. Safe because nothing scrolls under
     it here: below this row the main column and the rail scroll their own
     boxes (see THE MAIN COLUMN SCROLLS ITSELF). */
  .firma2-record-bar:not([data-idle]) {
    z-index: calc(var(--z-header, 200) + 2);
    background: transparent;
  }
  /* Optical edge: the icon buttons' 14px glyphs sit 9px inside their 32px
     boxes, so the cluster hangs out by that much and the last glyph lines up
     with the rail's content edge (the cards below), not its button box. */
  .firma2-record-bar__end {
    margin-inline-end: calc((2rem - 14px) / -2);
  }

  /* THE MAIN COLUMN SCROLLS ITSELF (user, 2026-10-22: "why not have the
     scroll bar of the main section to the left of the right side bar?").
     The pane used to scroll the whole page, so its one scrollbar ran down the
     window's edge on the far side of the rail — a bar for the document,
     drawn beyond a column that does not move with it. With a record bar the
     page below it is a fixed frame instead: the track under the bar
     (`.sidebar`) is exactly the fold's height, its content column scrolls on
     its own, and the rail scrolls its own inner box (firma2-rail), so each
     column's scrollbar is at its own trailing edge — the document's sits in
     the gutter left of the rail. Not while the rail is unpinned (tablet,
     phone): there the bar is idle, the rail is a block under the content,
     and the pane scrolls the lot as before. */
  :global(.esa-app-shell__content:has(> .firma2-record-bar:not([data-idle])) > .sidebar) {
    block-size: calc(var(--firma2-fold, 100dvh) - var(--firma2-band-height, 48px) - var(--firma2-record-bar-height, 2.5rem));
    /* Down through the pane's bottom padding, so the column scrolls to the
       pane's own foot rather than stopping a padding short of it. */
    margin-block-end: calc(var(--firma2-pane-padding, var(--spacing-500, 1.5rem)) * -1);
  }
  :global(.esa-app-shell__content:has(> .firma2-record-bar:not([data-idle])) > .sidebar > :not([data-rail], script, template, style)) {
    block-size: 100%;
    min-block-size: 0;
    /* A scroll box must be positioned, or absolutely placed descendants —
       visually-hidden labels, closed toolbars — take the pane as their
       containing block and stretch it into a second scrollbar. */
    position: relative;
    overflow-y: auto;
    overscroll-behavior: contain;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding-block-end: var(--firma2-pane-padding, var(--spacing-500, 1.5rem));
    /* THE SCROLLBAR SITS ON THE NEXT EDGE, NOT THE TEXT'S (user, 2026-10-23:
       "when the right side bar [closes] the scroll bar of the main section
       should be all the way to the right"). The box reaches through the
       sidebar's gutter to the rail, and padding hands the gutter back, so the
       text stays put and only the bar moves. Rail closed, the same reach lands
       on the sheet's edge: the collapsed rail keeps its bleed through the
       pane's padding, so the track already runs there. The pages give this box a bare
       <div> around their EsaContainer for the same reason: the container is
       capped and centred, and a capped scroll box draws its bar at the cap. */
    --_reach: var(--gap, var(--spacing-500, 1.5rem));
    margin-inline-end: calc(var(--_reach) * -1);
    padding-inline-end: var(--_reach);
  }
</style>
